      "problem": "Evaluate $(1 - 3\\,\\textrm{i})(2 + 4\\, \\textrm{i}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying two complex numbers is similar to multiplying two binomials. We also use the fact that $\\textrm{i}^2 = -1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1-3\\,\\text{i})(2+4\\,\\text{i}) & =1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4\\,\\text{i}+(-3\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 2+(-3\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 4\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =2+4\\,\\text{i}-6\\,\\text{i}-12\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =2-2\\,\\text{i}-12\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2-2\\,\\text{i}+12 \\\\  & =14-2\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
